      "body": "\n\n## Overview\n\nFix the `'_' allowed only in math mode` warning in `docs/design/hybrid_kv_cache_manager.md`.\n\n## Claims\n\n- Removes the docs build warning caused by unescaped underscores inside `\\text{}` in the page size formulas.\n- Both formulas (`page_size` and `page_size_bytes`) now render as code blocks.\n\n## Validation\n\nDocs-only change. Verified that the code blocks render correctly in GitHub's markdown preview. Relying on the PR docs build check for the full MkDocs build.\n\n## Details\n\nThe `\\text{num_layers}`, `\\text{block_size}` and `\\text{kv_hidden_size}` terms used bare underscores in LaTeX text mode, which KaTeX rejects. Rather than escaping them, I replaced both formulas with fenced code blocks. This avoids the LaTeX issue entirely.\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary> Pull Request Checklist </summary>\n\n- [ ] I used vLLM's `/pr-checklist` skill. (Mandatory for agents, optional for humans).\n- [x] AI assistance was used during the creation of this PR.\n\n- [x] **Design Fit:** Minimizes impact on core components, reuses existing functionality, and justifies added complexity.\n- [x] **Testing and Validation:** Validates the change and ensures any added tests are meaningful and reliable, with CI coverage or documented CI resource constraints and validation performed outside CI.\n- [x] **Code Quality and Style:** Keeps code and comments clear and concise, and updates relevant documentation and examples.\n- [x] **Pull Request Contents:** Includes a brief summary and relevant links, supports claims with evidence, explains root causes and implementation trade-offs, and follows the contributing guide.\n</details>\n\n<!-- codesmith:footer -->\n---\n<a href=\"https://app.blacksmith.sh/vllm-project/codesmith/vllm/pr/63717?autoLogin=true&ref=codesmith_pr_footer\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/view-with-codesmith-dark-v3.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-colo